<section class="chapter" aria-label="Shared architecture">
  <div class="chapter__inner">
    <h2 class="section-title">Shared Architecture</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      <b>Tools are the interface. The system is the operating model.</b>
      One shared layer of signals, logic, and guardrails runs across tools — so decisions stay consistent, work routes correctly, and automation remains reviewable.
    </p>

    <div class="grid3" aria-label="Architecture blocks">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Signals</h3>
        <p class="muted">Comparable inputs captured across workflows so drift, bottlenecks, and impact can be measured consistently.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Throughput, pass-through, and SLAs</li>
          <li>Open-text themes and reasons</li>
          <li>Capacity constraints across recruiter, hiring manager, and interview loops</li>
          <li>Risk indicators and drift signals</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Decision Logic</h3>
        <p class="muted">Rules that turn signals into action — with thresholds, tradeoffs, and escalation paths made explicit.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Expected ranges and alert thresholds</li>
          <li>Root-cause prompts</li>
          <li>Recommended actions and tradeoffs</li>
          <li>Escalation as stakes increase</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Execution</h3>
        <p class="muted">Actions happen inside the tools — and every action is visible, logged, and attributable.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Receipts attached to recommendations</li>
          <li>Approvals where needed</li>
          <li>Action logs and change history</li>
          <li>Clear "why this happened" context</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" aria-label="Operating loop">
  <div class="chapter__inner">
    <h2 class="section-title">The Operating Loop</h2>
    <p class="muted">The system only works if insight turns into action and outcomes feed the model back.</p>

    <div class="grid3" aria-label="Operating loop blocks">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Interpret</h3>
        <p class="muted">Signals are normalized and evaluated against shared definitions and expected ranges.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Metrics stay comparable</li>
          <li>Drift becomes visible</li>
          <li>Signal quality improves over time</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Route</h3>
        <p class="muted">The system decides whether to monitor, recommend, auto-execute, or escalate.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Low-risk work moves fast</li>
          <li>Higher-stakes decisions route to humans</li>
          <li>Escalation is rule-based, not improvised</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Learn</h3>
        <p class="muted">Outcomes feed back into the operating model so tools do not drift apart over time.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Closed-loop learning</li>
          <li>Threshold refinement</li>
          <li>Change control over shared logic</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      Most AI pilots fail because they stop at visibility. A real system closes the loop from signal → decision → action → learning.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

